## A small beginning

LUI is an application framework for Luau. Describe your interface with Instances, properties and events. LUI handles layout and lifetime; a native host displays your app.

{{Code:First-03-Event:Main.luau}}

You can start with the Windows SDK and VS Code. The SDK includes the command-line tools, native host, checker, layout inspector and editor extension. You do not need to build LUI from source to follow the tutorials.

## Find what you need

- [API reference](/LUI/docs/sdk-0.1.0-preview.1/api/): classes, services, types, constructors and helpers.
- [Everyday workflow](/LUI/docs/sdk-0.1.0-preview.1/guides/workflow/): check, run, inspect and come back later.
- [Setup help](/LUI/docs/sdk-0.1.0-preview.1/guides/setup/): download checks and common problems.
- [Platform support](/LUI/docs/sdk-0.1.0-preview.1/guides/platforms/): tested configurations and current limits.

## Help shape LUI

Suggestions and bug reports are welcome in [GitHub issues](https://github.com/gmoddev/LUI/issues). LUI is changing quickly, so pull requests and code contributions are paused for now. See the [contribution guide](https://github.com/gmoddev/LUI/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md).
